{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Extract the gate read-root/session domain out of llm/config.py\n\n## Context / Problem\n`src/rebar/llm/config.py` is at 793 LOC against the absolute 800 cap, so SEVEN lines of headroom, and\nit is the most CENTRAL near-cap file in the repo (fan-in 93). Ticket d23e's entire scope is this file\n— a `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` deprecation alias, which must keep honouring the old name, warn, and prefer the\nnew. MEASURED comparable: the `REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS` tombstone (`3eb3e71337`) cost +8 lines, and an\nalias is strictly bigger than a tombstone, so realistically 10-16 lines. Per-knob cost in this file is\nMEASURED at 10-13 lines. d23e is genuinely blocked.\n\n## Approach\n**ADR 0056 §Decision 5 pre-diagnosed this file and its prescription does NOT hold. Do not follow it.**\nIt said config.py's problem is \"178 lines of FLAT independent env reads\" wanting \"a declarative field\ntable\". Verified against the tree:\n * The SPAN claim holds (`from_env` is `config.py:575-753` = 179 lines) but the characterisation does\n   not. Only 125 of those lines are the flat `return cls(...)`; the other 53 are an ORDERING-COUPLED\n   preamble (the tombstone raise at `:581-584` must precede everything; `table`/`cli` must precede\n   every read; `current_code_root()` must beat the env var, `:617-625`). Of 29 kwargs, 22 are regular\n   and SEVEN are irregular (a derived non-knob `runner`; `api_key` env-only by secret policy; a 3-way\n   `repo_path` cascade rooted in a ContextVar; `tickets_path` with no env var at all; 20 lines of\n   custom `mcp_servers` JSON parsing; a nested `LangfuseConfig`; an enum-validating `overlap_drain`),\n   plus two field/env/file name mismatches a convention-driven table cannot derive.\n * **A TABLE WOULD BREAK THE ENV-VAR DRIFT GATE — this is the crux.** `scripts/gen_env_registry.py`\n   is a pure AST walk with no name resolution: it recognises a read only when the name argument is a\n   STRING LITERAL (`:117-124`) and files anything else under \"dynamically-constructed reads\", where\n   the variable DISAPPEARS from the table. A loop over spec rows makes that argument an\n   `ast.Attribute`, so all 19 currently-resolved rows vanish from `docs/env-vars.md` and CI fails.\n   `tests/unit/test_llm_config_pointer.py:259-267` exists to catch this class and names the precedent\n   (\"exactly what happened on sibling task f844\"); `llm/model_classes.py:112-130` spells out nine\n   literal `os.environ.get` calls rather than one indirection for the same reason. **The repo has\n   already tried the table shape here and rejected it.**\n * In-file, a table nets roughly ZERO lines anyway (~66 lines of rows replacing ~110, plus ~20 of\n   dispatch). It relieves nothing.\n\n**What the ADR missed, and what this ticket does instead: 219 of the 793 lines are not configuration\nat all.** `config.py:51-152` and `:190-269` are the gate read-root / snapshot-session domain — four\nContextVars and eleven functions (`current_code_root`, `resolve_code_root`, `current_tickets_root`,\n`current_code_sha`, `in_gate_session`, `gate_session`, `assert_gated`, `use_code_root`,\n`use_tickets_root`). `assert_gated` (`:216-240`) raises about `rebar.llm.gate_source` — it is a\nRUNTIME FAIL-CLOSED SECURITY GUARD, not a config knob.\n\nThree properties make this the right cut rather than a mechanical carve:\n 1. **The seam already has a consumer proving it real.** `llm/gate_source.py:35` imports exactly\n    `gate_session, use_code_root, use_tickets_root`, and its module docstring (`:1-18`) already\n    documents the block being moved.\n 2. **The domain is INERT.** All 154 lines of gate-context growth landed in five commits on or before\n    2026-07-09; ZERO since. Every commit after that date landed in the knob region. So this moves\n    cold mass out of the way of the hot region.\n 3. **One-way dependency, no cycle.** `gate_context` needs only stdlib + `rebar.config` + a lazy\n    `rebar.llm.errors`; it imports NOTHING from `llm.config`. `llm.config` imports it at module scope\n    for `from_env`. This respects `model_classes.py:16-20`'s rule that config must never import back.\n\nLEAVE `config.py:155-187` (`_active_gate_config`, `gate_config`, `resolve_gate_config`) IN PLACE — it\nis genuinely about `LLMConfig` and moving it buys a lazy import for no benefit.\n\n**HONEST LIMIT, state it in the change and the ADR: this RELOCATES MASS, it does NOT REMOVE THE\nABSORBER.** The absorber is the ~10-13 line per-knob cost in `from_env`, and the only structural fix\nfor that is blocked by the scanner. This buys about 15 knobs of runway, not permanence. The durable\nfollow-ups are (a) teach `gen_env_registry.py` to consume an exported spec list — precedent exists at\n`:150-160` where it already imports and unions `rebar._deprecations.REGISTRY` — and only THEN table-ify,\nor (b) domain-split the knobs per feature cluster (the 12 `overlap_*` fields are ~115 lines but change\n`cfg.overlap_k` to `cfg.overlap.k` at ~31 sites). Both are separate epics.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/llm/config.py` — remove `:51-152` and `:190-269`; add a re-export block.\n- `src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py` — NEW, ~202 LOC (clears the 100-LOC floor).\n- `docs/env-vars.md` — one regenerated cell: `REBAR_GATE_ALLOW_UNGATED` moves file (`config.py:227`).\n- `tests/unit/` — the headroom guard.\n\n## Testing\n**The relocation must require ZERO test edits. A required edit means the cut is wrong.**\nTHE RULE THAT MAKES THAT TRUE: re-export the moved names from `llm.config` and repoint NO consumer in\n`src/`. 13 monkeypatch targets name a moved symbol, and every consumer of `current_code_sha` /\n`assert_gated` uses a FUNCTION-LEVEL `from rebar.llm.config import ...` (verified at `attest.py:123`,\n`:251`, `:429`, `sidecar.py:404`, `runner.py:259`), so the name is resolved in `config`'s globals at\ncall time — exactly what `monkeypatch.setattr` rebinds. Repointing a consumer while a test patches\n`rebar.llm.config.<name>` is the silent-break mode ADR 0056 warns about.\n\nLoud canaries, which fail at COLLECTION if the re-export is wrong:\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_pass1_fanout_gate_session.py:19` and\n`tests/unit/test_code_review_gate_session.py:27` both do a module-scope\n`from rebar.llm.config import <moved name>`. `tests/unit/test_provider_session_guard.py:173` patches\n`llm_config.assert_gated` and fails loudly if the rebind stops taking effect.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `src/rebar/llm/config.py` is at or below 640 LOC and `src/rebar/llm/gate_context.py` is at least\n      100 and under 800\n- [ ] the seam guard for `llm/config.py` is TIGHTENED from the staged `<= 800` that sibling d8ef\n      introduces to the `< 700` policy target, in this same change — the change that creates the\n      headroom is the one that may assert it. (d8ef ships the staged bound because config.py is 793\n      today; do not re-add a guard, tighten the existing one in\n      `tests/unit/test_plan_review_workflow_ops_seam.py`.)\n- [ ] the full suite passes with ZERO edits to any existing test file\n- [ ] no module under `src/` imports the moved names from `gate_context` — every consumer still reaches\n      them through `rebar.llm.config`, so the monkeypatch targets keep working\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py` leaves the tree clean, with the moved\n      `REBAR_GATE_ALLOW_UNGATED` row regenerated rather than hand-edited\n- [ ] the NEW module's docstring states, IN-REPO, that this relocates inert mass and does NOT remove\n      the per-knob absorber in `from_env` — so the next reader sizing up config.py's growth curve\n      meets that caveat in the code rather than in a ticket they will not read\n- [ ] [operator-attested] the same caveat appears in the Gerrit commit message. Tagged because the\n      completion verifier reads repository files ONLY and cannot read git history, so a criterion\n      about a commit message is unconfirmable from the codebase and would burn a close cycle"}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785572873943691001,"uuid":"34eb1a21-6a8a-4414-9318-d4876b57a37f"}